# Docker Enterprise Registry

Purpose:
  Docker Enterprise Registry

Skill: Docker Enterprise Registry

ID:
  SKILL-PLAT-DOCKER-L4

Domain:
  platforms/docker

Use:
  managing enterprise Docker registries and supply chain

Apply:
  lead
  architect
  devops
  enterprise

Requires:
  SKILL-PLAT-DOCKER-L3
  registry-management
  security-scanning
  ci-cd

Avoid:
  public-registry-for-secrets
  unsigned-images
  no-vulnerability-scan
  missing-provenance

Level:
  L4

Status:
  EXPERIMENTAL

Maturity:
  VALIDATED

Risk:
  MEDIUM

Review:
  2026-08

Version:
  1.0

EvidenceLevel:
  HIGH

SearchKeys:
  docker
  registry
  enterprise
  supply chain
  security
  sigstore
  provenance

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/platforms/docker/L4-enterprise-registry.md

Evidence:
  - Docker Registry Documentation
  - Sigstore Documentation
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [D1] Use private registry (Harbor, ECR, GCR, ACR).
  [D2] Scan all images for vulnerabilities (Trivy, Grype).
  [D3] Sign images with Sigstore/Cosign.
  [D4] Use provenance attestations for supply chain.
  [D5] Implement registry access controls.
  [D6] Use image retention policies.
  [D7] Cache images in registry mirrors.
  [D8] Use SBOM (Software Bill of Materials).

Pros:
  - Secure supply chain
  - Compliance
  - Audit trail

Cons:
  - Operational overhead
  - Cost
  - Complexity

Alternatives:
  - GHCR (GitHub)
  - Docker Hub (cloud)
  - AWS ECR

State: +

